Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching Quantum Things: A Build-It-Yourself Catalog of Open-System \
Simulations\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
A single, self-contained tour of twenty small open quantum systems, from \
master equations for the unconditioned average to monitored trajectories and \
feedback, each built from plain matrices, computed on the spot, and shown as \
a picture.\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami", "Author",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Wolfram Research, Inc.", "Affiliation",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Catalog Flows", "Subsection",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["\<\
This is a hands-on tour of open quantum systems: systems that leak energy or \
information to their environment, watched by a detector on the output. We \
build a driven atom relaxing to its steady state, light in a leaky cavity, a \
superposition that decoheres almost the instant it forms, an atom whose \
fluorescence we read first as single photons and then as a homodyne current, \
a mechanical resonator cooled by measurement and feedback, and a dozen more. \
Each becomes a few lines of code you can run and change, and each ends in a \
picture.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
I strongly believe in a computation-first way of learning: in a sense, if I \
cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand it. Real understanding shows \
up when you can actually do the thing, simulate it, predict it, watch it, not \
when you can only repeat words about it. So the rhythm here is always the \
same: say an idea in plain words, say it again more plainly, compute it, look \
at what came out, and let that raise the next question.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell["\<\
Two notes on style. First, the file stands on its own: no other document, \
textbook, or note is needed. Second, I use the standard names (density \
matrix, Bloch vector, master equation, dissipator, coherent state) and \
explain each in one plain sentence the first time it appears; the code uses \
the same standard names, so it reads like the physics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["\<\
The thing you are reading is a live notebook. Evaluate the cells from top to \
bottom, because later cells lean on earlier ones. My suggestion is to look at \
each output and what it means before picking apart the code that made it. And \
you are not locked into anything: change a number, watch a different system, \
reseed the randomness, and see what moves. That is the whole point.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["What You Need, and How to Read This", "Subsection",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You need three ideas. First, the state is a ",
 StyleBox["density matrix",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ": an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " Hermitian matrix (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " = number of levels, 2 for a qubit, more for an oscillator), with the level \
populations on its diagonal (summing to one) and the coherences off-diagonal. \
Second, the system has a Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " that drives its unitary evolution when left alone. Third, one random \
quantity recurs below: the Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 ", a Gaussian random step with variance equal to the time step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ". Where the pace steepens I will say so."
}], "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " throughout, so every rate and frequency is in units of inverse time."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["The Toolkit: Everything the Twenty Examples Share", "Section",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["\<\
Before any specific system, we build the small set of tools every example \
reuses. There are about ten of them, each a few lines. Once they are in hand, \
each of the twenty systems is just a short setup, a run, a picture, and a \
check.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell["The density matrix, and quantities read from it", "Subsection",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The smallest system is a qubit. Everything is built from the three Pauli \
matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " identity:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}], " ", 
   "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "j", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The basis states are the excited state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "1", ",", "0", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " and the ground state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "0", ",", "1", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 "; their equal superposition is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], "+", 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
    SqrtBox["2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"excited", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ground", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"plus", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The lowering operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " takes the excited state to the ground state (an atom emitting a photon). \
Build it from the Pauli matrices:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lower", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"X", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "Y"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check that it sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "excited"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It lands on the ground state. Its conjugate transpose is the raising \
operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ", written inline when needed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A state vector describes only a pure state. The general state, pure or \
mixed, is the density matrix; for a pure state it is the outer product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "v_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "v", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell["Form the density matrix of the excited state:", "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " this is a single 1 in the top corner."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two quantities summarize any qubit state. The first is the ",
 StyleBox["Bloch vector",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ": it has length 1 for a pure state and shrinks as the state mixes. Define \
it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " points along the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 "-axis:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
  RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It points along the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 "-axis, length one."
}], "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second quantity is the ",
 StyleBox["purity",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ": 1 for a pure state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " for the maximally mixed qubit. Define it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell["Read it for a pure state and for the maximally mixed one:", "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", 
    RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", 
    RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell["\<\
The pure state gives one, the maximally mixed state one half.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Last, the ",
 StyleBox["expectation value",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"A", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " of any operator, which predicts what a meter reads:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"expectation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"op_", ",", " ", "rho_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"op", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell["The two terms of the master equation", "Subsection",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A state changes for two reasons. The first is unitary evolution under the \
Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 ": the commutator term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ". Define it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"commutatorTerm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H_", ",", " ", "rho_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"H", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "H"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second is a leak to the environment, one Lindblad (jump) operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " per channel (for a decaying atom, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 "). Its ",
 StyleBox["dissipator",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " transfers population along the channel and damps coherences, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"c_", ",", " ", "rho_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"c", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "c", "]"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "c", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "c", 
        " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "c", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "c"}]}],
       ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A dissipator is trace-preserving, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 ", so the total probability stays one. Confirm it for a general ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
   RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c11", ",", " ", "c12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c21", ",", " ", "c22"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r11", ",", " ", "r12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r21", ",", " ", "r22"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell["Zero with no assumptions.", "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Together the two terms give the ",
 StyleBox["Lindblad master equation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 ", the evolution of an open system averaged over all measurement outcomes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"lindbladian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H_", ",", " ", "leaks_List", ",", " ", "rho_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"commutatorTerm", "[", 
     RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "rho"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      "leaks"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is a system that leaks but is not watched: smooth and deterministic, \
because averaging over every detector outcome removes the randomness. The \
first several examples are this equation with different ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " and leaks."
}], "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell["The master equation, solved two independent ways", "Subsection",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We solve the master equation two independent ways and check they agree. The \
first vectorizes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " (stack its rows) and applies the ",
 StyleBox["Liouvillian",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", the matrix whose action is ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 ". In this row-stacking convention (matching WL's ",
 Cell[BoxData["Flatten"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox["", "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " the entrywise conjugate) it is the Kronecker form"
}], "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "\[CircleTimes]", "\|01d7d9", "-", "\|01d7d9",
     "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["[",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "_"], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", "\|01d7d9", "+", "\|01d7d9", "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["]",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which the code builds equivalently by feeding ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " each basis matrix and stacking the results:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H_", ",", " ", "leaks_List", ",", " ", "d_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "e", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
         RowBox[{"lindbladian", "[", 
          RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "leaks", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"d", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", "e"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"e", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"d", "^", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " is then a matrix exponential of the Liouvillian applied to the vectorized \
initial state, reshaped back to a matrix, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["vec",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], " ", 
   StyleBox["vec",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H_", ",", " ", "leaks_List", ",", " ", "rho0_", ",", " ", "t_"}],
     "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "rho0", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
           RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "leaks", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"N", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
         RowBox[{"N", "@", "rho0"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Liouvillian also gives the ",
 StyleBox["steady state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["ss",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 ", satisfying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["ss",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 ": the null space of the Liouvillian (there can be more than one), \
normalized to unit trace:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H_", ",", " ", "leaks_List"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ns", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"NullSpace", "[", 
        RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
         RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "leaks", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "H", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "H", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "H", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
        " ", "/@", " ", "ns"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell["\<\
The second way integrates the master equation directly with an ODE solver, \
sharing no code with the Liouvillian route:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "H_", ",", " ", "leaks_List", ",", " ", "rho0_", ",", " ", "t1_"}], "]"}],
    " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"s", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lindbladian", "[", 
         RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "leaks", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"s", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "@", "rho0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "t1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the cross-check. Fix a test system: a qubit driven by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ", dephased through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 ", starting in the ground state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Hx", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1.0", " ", "X"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"oneLeak", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "0.4", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"start", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ground", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell["Integrate its master equation once with the ODE route:", "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solved", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Hx", ",", " ", "oneLeak", ",", " ", "start", ",", " ", "10.0"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell["\<\
Measure the largest disagreement between the two solvers over the whole span:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "Hx", ",", " ", "oneLeak", ",", " ", "start", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}],
        " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"solved", "[", "tt", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "10", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell["\<\
The largest disagreement is at the ODE solver's tolerance: the matrix \
exponential and the ODE march give the same state. Either is a trustworthy \
reference.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell["The positivity-preserving measurement step", "Subsection",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now put a detector on a leak and condition the state on its output. The \
naive update, nudging ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " by the record, can push ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 " off the set of valid states and give a negative eigenvalue, a negative \
probability. See it break: take ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 ", measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " with no Hamiltonian, and feed one large noise kick into the naive update:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"naiveStep", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Z", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "0.1"}], 
    " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Z", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "Z"}], 
       " ", "-", "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "Z"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     "0.5"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell["Read the smallest eigenvalue of the updated state:", "Text",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "naiveStep", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A negative eigenvalue: the naive update has left the set of valid states. \
Shrinking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " makes it rarer but never impossible."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fix is the structure-preserving filter of ",
 ButtonBox["Rouchon and Ralph (2015)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.5345"], None}],
 ": write the update as a sum of Kraus terms ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 ", an operator times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " times its conjugate transpose, so the result is manifestly positive at any \
step size. With monitored operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " at detection efficiencies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 ", unmonitored leaks ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["l", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ", record increments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ", the no-jump generator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "+", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["l", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["l", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 ", and the measurement kick ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 ", the corrected Kraus operator is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "=", "\|01d7d9", "-", 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"], "2"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell["and the stepped state is the renormalized sum", "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["l", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["l", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three terms of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 " are the measured record, the unmonitored leaks, and the unrecorded \
fraction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 " of each watched channel; each has Kraus form, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 " stays valid for any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 ", and averaging over the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " recovers the Lindblad master equation. Build it: it takes the fixed model \
pieces and returns a function mapping a state and a record to the next \
state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"measurementStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "H_", ",", " ", "watched_List", ",", " ", "effs_List", ",", " ", 
     "unwatched_List", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"id", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "H", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"drift", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"I", " ", "H"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
             RowBox[{"watched", ",", " ", "unwatched"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
          "2"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"corr", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
          RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"#1", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"#2", " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"effs", ",", " ", "watched"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "/",
          "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "dJ"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"sig", ",", " ", "M", ",", " ", "top"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
         "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"sig", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
            RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#2", "]"}], " ", "#1", " ", "#3"}], " ",
                "&"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"dJ", ",", " ", "effs", ",", " ", "watched"}], "}"}]}],
              "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"M", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"id", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"drift", " ", "dt"}], " ", "+", " ", "sig", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"sig", " ", ".", " ", "sig"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"corr", " ", "dt"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"top", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"M", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "M", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", 
            "       ", 
            RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], 
               " ", "/@", " ", "unwatched"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", 
            "       ", 
            RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ")"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"#1", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}]}], " ", 
                 "&"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"watched", ",", " ", "effs"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
              "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"top", "/", 
           RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
            RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "top", "]"}]}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 Cell[BoxData["watched"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 " are the monitored channels, ",
 Cell[BoxData["effs"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " their detection efficiencies (1 for perfect, less if the detector misses \
some output), and ",
 Cell[BoxData["unwatched"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 " the undetected leaks. Revisit the kick that broke the naive step, now \
through the positivity-preserving step:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fixedStep", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measurementStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "Z", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "0.5", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell["\<\
Read the smallest eigenvalue and the trace of the stepped state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "fixedStep", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "fixedStep", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell["\<\
The smallest eigenvalue is now zero to rounding and the trace is one: the \
step lands on the boundary of the state space instead of leaving it. \
Positivity no longer depends on the step size.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell["The measurement record, and one trajectory", "Subsection",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The homodyne record at each step is the signal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " plus fresh Gaussian noise. Write it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"measurementRecord", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "rho_", ",", " ", "watched_List", ",", " ", "effs_List", ",", " ", "dt_", 
     ",", " ", "kick_List"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#3", "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".",
            " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}], " ", "dt"}], " ", "+", " ", "#2"}], " ", 
      "&"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"watched", ",", " ", "kick", ",", " ", "effs"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["kick"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " is the Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 ", drawn fresh each step. One ",
 StyleBox["quantum trajectory",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is: draw ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 ", form the record, advance with the positivity step. This is the only place \
randomness enters. It returns the times, the states, and the record:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "rho0_", ",", " ", "H_", ",", " ", "watched_List", ",", " ", "effs_List", 
     ",", " ", "unwatched_List", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "tf_", ",", " ", 
     "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
           RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "step", ",", " ", 
         "kicks", ",", " ", "states", ",", " ", "record"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"measurementStep", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "H", ",", " ", "watched", ",", " ", "effs", ",", " ", "unwatched", ",",
            " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"kicks", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dt", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "watched", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";",
         "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"states", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "dw"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"step", "[", 
              RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"measurementRecord", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                "r", ",", " ", "watched", ",", " ", "effs", ",", " ", "dt", ",",
                  " ", "dw"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "rho0", ",",
            " ", "kicks"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"record", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"measurementRecord", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "#1", ",", " ", "watched", ",", " ", "effs", ",", " ", "dt", ",",
               " ", "#2"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Most", "[", "states", "]"}], ",", " ", "kicks"}], 
            "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"<|", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\"\<times\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<states\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "states"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<record\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "record"}]}], "|>"}]}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell["\<\
The check that ties the catalog together: trajectories average to the master \
equation\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell["\<\
The central fact, used as a check almost everywhere: averaging many \
trajectories recovers the master-equation solution. Averaging over the record \
is what tracing out the detector means. Fix the step and the horizon:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "8.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["Run 200 trajectories of the test qubit:", "Text",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"crowd", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{"start", ",", " ", "Hx", ",", " ", "oneLeak", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "k"}], 
       "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "200"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell["Integrate the master equation as the reference:", "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"smoothRef", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"evolveODE", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Hx", ",", " ", "oneLeak", ",", " ", "start", ",", " ", "tf"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell["\<\
Measure the largest gap between the ensemble mean and that reference:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
      "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "crowd", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"smoothRef", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
            RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The gap is the Monte-Carlo scatter of a finite ensemble, shrinking as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 ". The trajectory ensemble and the master equation share no code yet agree: \
a numerical validation, repeated throughout, that a stochastic example is \
built right."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One more fact from the same run: each ",
 StyleBox["conditional",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " trajectory stays pure, while the ensemble average is mixed. Compare the \
purity of one trajectory's final state with that of the ensemble mean:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{"start", ",", " ", "Hx", ",", " ", "oneLeak", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "1"}], 
       "]"}], "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "crowd", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell["\<\
The single trajectory ends pure; the average ends mixed. This is the heart of \
the subject: under ideal monitoring (a pure initial state, every output \
channel watched, unit detector efficiency, no extra unrecorded noise) \
decoherence does not happen to any one conditioned state, which stays pure, \
and mixing is entirely the result of averaging over the unrecorded outcomes. \
Relax any of those conditions, add inefficiency, an unmonitored channel, \
thermal drive, or dephasing, and the conditioned state itself becomes mixed; \
the pure-trajectory picture is the ideal limit, and where the examples below \
invoke it they are in that limit.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell["The Bloch-sphere plot", "Subsection",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a qubit the natural picture is the Bloch sphere: the Bloch vector's tip \
lies on the surface for a pure state, inside for a mixed one. ",
 Cell[BoxData["BlochSpherePlot"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 " draws the labeled sphere:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bloch", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<BlochSpherePlot\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell["\<\
A small octahedron will mark where a trajectory ends; build it from its six \
vertices:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"diamond", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", " ", "r_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GraphicsComplex", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"p", " ", "+", " ", "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"r", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Polygon", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}],
     "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell["\<\
The plotter uses one visual grammar for every trajectory: the path is a \
curve, a small ball marks where it starts, a diamond marks where it ends, and \
all three share one color per trajectory. A label names the picture, a legend \
names the trajectories when they mean different things, and extra marks \
(fixed points, targets) ride along as plain graphics primitives:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{"paths_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"lbl_", " ", ":", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"names_", " ", ":", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"extras_", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"bloch", "[", "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
          RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
                RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"First", "@", "#2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "Thick", ",",
                " ", 
               RowBox[{"Line", "[", "#1", "]"}], ",", "\n", "         ", 
               RowBox[{"Sphere", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"First", "[", "#1", "]"}], ",", " ", "0.035"}], 
                "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"diamond", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Last", "[", "#1", "]"}], ",", " ", "0.06"}], 
                "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "paths"}], "]"}], "]"}],
          ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", "extras", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "lbl"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "340"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"names", " ", "===", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", "g", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Legended", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"LineLegend", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
              RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "names", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           "names"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell["Run one monitored trajectory of the test qubit:", "Text",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"demoRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Hx", ",", " ", 
     "oneLeak", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "3.0", ",", " ", "4"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell["\<\
Now visualize the monitored trajectory on the Bloch sphere, from its starting \
ball to its final diamond:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"demoRun", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", "\"\<one monitored trajectory, ball to diamond\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell["\<\
The Bloch vector wanders as the record comes in; one seed is one run. Change \
the seed and it wanders differently; averaging many recovers the smooth \
relaxation checked above.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell["\<\
The sphere shows the shape of the path; the same run also reads as three \
numbers in time, one curve for each Bloch component:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"demoRun", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Sigma]x\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Sigma]y\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Sigma]z\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Bloch component\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"MinMax", "@", 
     RowBox[{"demoRun", "[", "\"\<times\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the same run, component by component\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three components move. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 " starts at one and decays toward zero, since the drive turns the state \
about the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 "-axis and cannot rebuild what watching ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 " erases; meanwhile ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " wander as that same drive rotates them and the record tips the state \
toward a pole. The sphere and the curves are one trajectory seen two ways: \
the sphere gives the shape of the path, the curves give each direction \
changing in time. This component-by-component reading is how a watched qubit \
is usually plotted, and most later examples show just the one component the \
measurement makes interesting, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],
 " for a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 " measurement. With the qubit toolkit in hand, on to the first systems."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell["The same machinery, in standard notation", "Subsection",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every example below opens with a one-line statement of its problem in \
standard notation, so the formal problem and the plain solution sit side by \
side. It is only names for the machinery you just built. The state is the \
density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 "; the averaged evolution is the ",
 StyleBox["master equation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "whose Hamiltonian part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["commutatorTerm"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 " and each of whose dissipators"
}], "Text",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "is ",
 Cell[BoxData["dissipator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 ". For a qubit the ",
 StyleBox["Bloch vector",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\|01d7d9", "+", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "+", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "+", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 "; the lowering operator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 ", and for an oscillator the annihilation operator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 ". When the record is kept, ",
 Cell[BoxData["measurementStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " integrates a ",
 StyleBox["stochastic master equation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " whose measurement (diffusion) term for a monitored ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 ", driven by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 "; photon counting instead applies the jump ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d4a2", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "/", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 " at click times."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell["The Twenty Governing Equations, at a Glance", "Subsection",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is the dynamics of every example in one place. All stochastic \
equations are It\[OHat] equations. For a Hermitian observable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 " monitored through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], " ", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 ", the catalog uses"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "J"}], "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SqrtBox[
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       StyleBox["c", "TI"]], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 " is the coefficient carried by the monitored operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 " in the code. Equivalently, the rescaled record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

