     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the estimate rings down under the force it drives\>\""}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<estimated position\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<feedback force\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[246]:= ",
 CellID->1378080400,ExpressionUUID->"716ae4bc-5935-f42e-2769-fde658c1df74"],

Cell["\<\
The estimate rings down as the force pushes against it, the mechanical \
analogue of a shock absorber built from a measurement.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->880029775,ExpressionUUID->"59aa617b-186b-0315-0faa-7925991e6e7f"],

Cell["\<\
How hard should the loop push? Sweep the gain and read the steady occupation \
off the exact Lyapunov balance:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1216675886,ExpressionUUID->"008b4284-ba53-483f-3089-5bee3fe61b05"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gainsCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "12", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"gainsCool", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nUncCool", " ", "/@", " ", "gainsCool"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<feedback gain G\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steady phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<an optimal gain: too little leaves it warm, too much feeds \
noise back\>\""}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gainsCool"}], ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gainsCool"}], ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], 
          "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[247]:= ",
 CellID->764992932,ExpressionUUID->"3c0a4c18-9cc5-5190-640a-6642157023fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The occupation falls steeply from the heated open-loop value, reaches a \
minimum near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ec90d37-5b76-64dd-46f6-a5715e034e27"],
 ", then rises again: beyond the optimum the loop feeds the estimate's own \
measurement noise back onto the oscillator, the imprecision-back-action \
tradeoff that caps every real feedback-cooling experiment. It never reaches \
the conditional floor (green): that would need a noiseless actuator acting on \
a perfectly known state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->746121340,ExpressionUUID->"0f4a94b8-2093-0aa7-3549-0de25126588d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, a better detector lowers both the floor and the achievable cold. \
Repeat the floor-plus-spread Lyapunov balance at efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "746ef244-02b1-295f-1c15-f42eb7447ba5"],
 ", where the conditional covariance sharpens and the gain becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "k"}], "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalSigma]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16a579b4-853c-ad3d-3e5b-70fe2ccef407"],
 ", holding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d0d0eda-2f65-a967-6b32-a7844a11f84d"],
 " fixed at its ideal-detector value (not re-optimized per ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25424d11-215d-69ec-5372-655b50e83b36"],
 ", so the cooled curve is conservative at low ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38b2585b-f0b8-eb1e-6842-52048132b664"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1139255012,ExpressionUUID->"310aba1e-c173-53a6-6709-3c5bf006218c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nUncCoolEta", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]_", ",", " ", "gg_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "kx", ",", 
       " ", "kp", ",", " ", "s"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "kCool"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kp", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "kCool"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], 
           ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
              "gg"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kx", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kx", " ", "kp"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kx", " ", "kp"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kp", "^", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"s", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"c", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"c", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ",
        "0.5"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[248]:= ",
 CellID->965302876,ExpressionUUID->"6d663f9d-52b3-ad35-1b1d-b6c76747f41f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sweep the efficiency from a poor detector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae604be-6e2a-038b-3a9d-9df80bdf51d1"],
 ", to a perfect one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1302650277,ExpressionUUID->"5a3bb7fa-395b-d8d2-0bd8-2ea4b8efaa38"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"etasCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0.01"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[249]:= ",
 CellID->1688685886,ExpressionUUID->"77106238-91db-a6eb-1d2f-8462206f0c31"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the conditional floor and the fixed-gain cooled occupation against \
efficiency:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->632063892,ExpressionUUID->"01a00532-4a0e-3544-375f-9d7c6fb89fae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"etasCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", 
           " ", "0.5"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", " ", "/@", " ", "etasCool"}], ")"}]}]}], 
       "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"etasCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"nUncCoolEta", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "Gcool"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
         " ", "etasCool"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<conditional floor\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<cooled occupation (fixed gain)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<detector efficiency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<a better detector cools colder\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[250]:= ",
 CellID->1331054704,ExpressionUUID->"1f5de8ef-4b2e-05e8-4562-01c96edb6f32"],

Cell["\<\
Both curves fall as the detector improves, and the gap between them is the \
price of noisy actuation. This is measurement-based cooling of a \
nanomechanical drum or a levitated nanoparticle toward its ground state, not \
by contact with something colder but by watching precisely and pushing back: \
the same conditional covariance that told the Kalman filter how well it could \
track now sets how cold the feedback can pull.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1024214867,ExpressionUUID->"39671b4e-a434-cf2d-6f1c-932bcdc69277"],

Cell["Part Seven: Two Bookkeepings, and the Colour of the Light", "Section",
 CellID->509901081,ExpressionUUID->"1fdf432e-aa6d-b711-45e5-5a8bcf191a7b"],

Cell["Linear vs Nonlinear: One Trajectory, Two Descriptions", "Subsection",
 CellID->1957271700,ExpressionUUID->"6d59f3c2-2879-5f97-1b66-eaac490c25fd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " One diffusive history, written two equivalent ways. The ",
 StyleBox["linear", "TI"],
 " stochastic Schrodinger equation runs an unnormalized state under plain \
noise,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->935291515,ExpressionUUID->"2630e3fa-641e-82e1-4fcf-faa40da8d0cb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "=", 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->2045201311,ExpressionUUID->"448695d4-2f33-b50a-6cbd-0c9e4ac71c50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "whose squared norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleVerticalBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29c39546-676c-16ec-5ff0-0d2012197c36"],
 " is exactly the ",
 StyleBox["likelihood", "TI"],
 " of the record that drove it. The ",
 StyleBox["nonlinear", "TI"],
 " master equation instead carries the normalized state an experimenter \
tracks, driven not by that raw noise but by the ",
 StyleBox["innovation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f46310b-a697-198a-757d-a954d3226bd0"],
 ", the increment with the conditional mean it predicts removed,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->129431700,ExpressionUUID->"216d5a5a-69e9-2e30-5713-5c040f9c751a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     StyleBox["Re",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->359040978,ExpressionUUID->"1c61f6d7-23c3-7683-441e-ef9156765ce9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The startling fact is that the plain average of the ",
 StyleBox["unnormalized", "TI"],
 " states, with no reweighting at all, already is the master equation. Build \
the linear version and check."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1429785775,ExpressionUUID->"307817dd-a48d-ada0-6007-8e86cd39f78a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One diffusive trajectory has two equivalent descriptions. The ",
 StyleBox["nonlinear",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " SME (used so far) carries the normalized state and renormalizes each step. \
The ",
 StyleBox["linear",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " SSE evolves an unnormalized state under plain (unconditioned) noise, never \
renormalizing,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1008132517,ExpressionUUID->"4a8241cb-623a-869a-7ab2-589517ccece0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], "-", 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox["1", "2"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
      TemplateBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
       "Ket"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
       "Ket"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->764580650,ExpressionUUID->"367e3c7d-819a-afca-5e05-b627302cf510"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "its squared norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
   "BraKet"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78d621b8-eaa7-e995-28ed-b8e58f53bbff"],
 " the likelihood of the record. The striking fact: the plain average of the \
unnormalized outer products ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c3eb8ce-9873-62c7-05c5-31a81906302d"],
 ", unweighted, is already the master-equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73390226-095c-13d5-22c6-9b80a8e9613f"],
 ". Fix the atom and the non-Hermitian drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "242c2995-be92-4813-4dd3-c0df3b271b79"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->302184118,ExpressionUUID->"6cf9f011-b091-ff11-1486-ea5ac125c27b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"cLin", " ", "=", " ", "lower"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Knh", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], " ", "-", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cLin", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      "cLin"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"steps", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[251]:= ",
 CellID->1619716671,ExpressionUUID->"03763f09-e75f-2a04-310d-b75292ea796e"],

Cell["One unnormalized run under plain noise, never renormalizing:", "Text",
 CellID->1797210921,ExpressionUUID->"6d2ce3de-bdcd-8de8-14d3-fa983479d732"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"linearRun", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"Fold", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Knh", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "step"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cLin", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "#2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "excited", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "step", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "steps"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[252]:= ",
 CellID->454532135,ExpressionUUID->"037e6481-2025-8b3e-3106-7deb51d1d604"],

Cell["Run four hundred of them:", "Text",
 CellID->960455850,ExpressionUUID->"4ff4878c-0720-c57b-758b-1ed6b2daac41"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"linearStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linearRun", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "400", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[253]:= ",
 CellID->588212915,ExpressionUUID->"3d786225-2032-4147-6b18-7b8f51c713ad"],

Cell["Average the outer products, with no reweighting at all:", "Text",
 CellID->1438862008,ExpressionUUID->"775c6681-2d8b-f484-1d64-7feb443fdeee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"linearAverage", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", "linearStates"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[254]:= ",
 CellID->1022895307,ExpressionUUID->"75bb4ea4-bbde-cef1-2359-670e3e6894db"],

Cell["Measure the gap to the master equation:", "Text",
 CellID->424225543,ExpressionUUID->"6f77f163-25db-f065-150c-e94d4c6fc34f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{"linearAverage", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "cLin", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[255]:= ",
 CellID->1694748468,ExpressionUUID->"1c3c3f10-7538-8927-45c3-b75a7cb2d80d"],

Cell["\<\
The unweighted average matches the master equation to the Monte-Carlo \
scatter, with no renormalization.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->377500653,ExpressionUUID->"51549184-e5a4-8496-076b-08e18c56eefc"],

Cell["\<\
The squared norms are genuine likelihoods, so they average to one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->827200276,ExpressionUUID->"39696f27-c9aa-0144-6f16-8680e85f53ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", 
    "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[256]:= ",
 CellID->19958409,ExpressionUUID->"45dcfd53-12c9-ed0c-73e3-f51da77db456"],

Cell["Different records carry different weight.", "Text",
 CellID->2075932104,ExpressionUUID->"43afbe7d-b702-93ca-7154-3026c2b4e110"],

Cell["Now visualize the distribution of their likelihood weights:", "Text",
 CellID->467824327,ExpressionUUID->"143db07b-777b-32d6-3dc2-2a25020f803c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ",
      "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}], ",", " ", "30", ",", 
   " ", "\"\<PDF\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<likelihood weight\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the likelihood weights average to one\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[257]:= ",
 CellID->1012559019,ExpressionUUID->"78b7e50c-4773-01ae-284c-fd56720653f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These are two faithful descriptions of the same diffusive process, related \
by a change of probability measure. Renormalize the state each step and feed \
the record back into the drift, and you get the physical (nonlinear) state an \
experimenter tracks in real time. Evolve the unnormalized state under plain, \
unconditioned noise and never renormalize, and you get the linear picture, \
often easier to simulate. The linear state's ",
 StyleBox["direction", "TI"],
 " still fluctuates with the noise; what the weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleVerticalBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68443c72-a4f0-9c3e-187b-b63fcc8ae704"],
 " isolates is not the randomness but the physical likelihood of each record, \
the Girsanov factor that turns the reference measure into the physical one."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1427622929,ExpressionUUID->"445c0952-f215-e20d-6c63-a11f87a1b157"],

Cell["\<\
One record carries both bookkeepings at once. Roll out a single linear run \
keeping its whole history:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->115085158,ExpressionUUID->"3a680f33-ae9a-dfdd-6a17-a77ccb2ca527"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Knh", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "step"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cLin", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "#2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "excited", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "step", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "steps"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oneA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", "[", "7", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gridA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"step", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "steps"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[258]:= ",
 CellID->2053577179,ExpressionUUID->"3043dcf6-9c3e-c649-6070-d5b015c8ac93"],

Cell["\<\
Read the two descriptions off that one run: the normalized state (the \
physical trajectory you would track) and the log-weight it accumulates (its \
likelihood score), on aligned axes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->248898466,ExpressionUUID->"32a697fb-66fd-3c96-625d-0ea5128986fc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gridA5", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "Z", 
                  " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", 
             "&"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
           " ", "oneA5"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
        RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<excited population (normalized)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the state you track\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gridA5", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], 
             "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "oneA5"}]}], "}"}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
        RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "All"}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<log weight  log \[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]\[Psi]\
\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(\), \(2\)]\)\>\""}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the likelihood it carries\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[259]:= ",
 CellID->538674263,ExpressionUUID->"6e733b29-d0f2-c400-1600-b372e084af6a"],

Cell["\<\
The same record has a normalized-state reading and a running weight; neither \
alone is the trajectory, together they are.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1089240833,ExpressionUUID->"0249f5b1-f79b-eab1-3276-ecfa822fb89b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The catch of the linear method is that the weights spread, so a handful of \
records come to dominate the average, the importance-sampling degeneracy. \
Measure it with the effective sample size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["eff",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Sum]",
       FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
      StyleBox["w", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Sum]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d8d8362-02d3-9c7f-2bb2-1b4cb767e745"],
 " across the ensemble over time:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1426757747,ExpressionUUID->"16d64695-ef97-7390-3eee-5fde8a2241fa"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"essPathsA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "400", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"essA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], 
               "]"}], " ", "&"}], "@", 
             RowBox[{"#", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
          " ", "essPathsA5"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "400."}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steps", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "20"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"gridA5", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "20"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", "essA5"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
     RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<effective sample size / N\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the linear weights degenerate: fewer records carry the \
average\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[260]:= ",
 CellID->892816339,ExpressionUUID->"492272d1-18a5-64bf-78d2-6b9b99504e85"],

Cell["\<\
The effective fraction falls from one toward a fraction of the ensemble: as \
time goes on, the unweighted linear average is carried by ever fewer \
high-weight records, and its Monte-Carlo error grows even though it remains \
unbiased. That is the price of the linear picture's convenience, and the \
reason the nonlinear (renormalized) equation, which keeps every trajectory \
equally weighted, is what a long real-time filter uses.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1017845166,ExpressionUUID->"1f8fc6a3-d6eb-41c0-45b4-df0ce29e132a"],

Cell["The Driven Atom, Averaged and Watched", "Subsection",
 CellID->649399840,ExpressionUUID->"740a6ce3-9f6e-a7ea-1c09-85cd1a180d30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The fully worked driven, damped, emitting atom, both averaged and watched. \
In full generality its unconditional master equation carries detuning, \
thermal drive, and pure dephasing,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->95053520,ExpressionUUID->"355eb3db-64ad-28a6-6365-2a850d587a8c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[Hacek]"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], " ", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], " ", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[Hacek]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->823893091,ExpressionUUID->"224bec90-94dc-e798-5248-05da1d6ecde2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and relaxes to a mixed steady state inside the ball. We take the standard \
resonance-fluorescence corner, resonant (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19da10ea-d928-9e66-4ff9-89b7d8c2e54c"],
 "), zero temperature (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cf78db7-632c-d0e2-148c-24f116dea2c8"],
 "), no extra dephasing (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "634058bc-0e0e-c957-1170-51e6abb89bbd"],
 "), which reduces it to a single emission channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187ea1f6-0b66-2b61-4805-38b0ae13764b"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->973753736,ExpressionUUID->"6a5920d9-eb16-a7a4-1a66-b9828ea00d8e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->308061613,ExpressionUUID->"09f2771d-8da8-86b6-3f82-6f472442ec9c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watching that one channel with unit efficiency keeps the conditioned \
history pure on the surface of the ball; the record-blind average is the \
mixed interior point. Compare the two. (Restore any of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2eae7486-c77b-107a-5656-6de3f20e6340"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58a71232-b93f-0bc4-085c-947c38ca592e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0590db7a-de3c-d1b6-33af-d327dbcea39c"],
 " and the conditioned state would itself become mixed, since a thermal or \
dephasing channel is then present and unmonitored.)"
}], "Text",
 CellID->218833087,ExpressionUUID->"2f6adbb8-aab7-c223-5569-d2e5cf439109"],

Cell["\<\
Pull the threads together on one worked example: a driven, emitting atom. \
Averaged (unconditioned), it relaxes to a mixed steady state inside the Bloch \
ball. Fix the atom and compute its steady Bloch vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1362785884,ExpressionUUID->"360b7cf2-7095-e6b8-5e09-75bc0121cc82"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", " ", "=", " ", "3."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"settled", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
    RowBox[{"First", "@", 
     RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", "/", "2"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]dr", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[261]:= ",
 CellID->800074720,ExpressionUUID->"571ae662-c9c7-b1ca-7d39-f84fe8730310"],

Cell["Read its length (a pure state has length one):", "Text",
 CellID->154434508,ExpressionUUID->"45b5dbb0-b576-45eb-734a-d2fa3c032f31"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "settled", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[262]:= ",
 CellID->1025583273,ExpressionUUID->"4ce9c8c0-fe52-3cd7-7496-e1adfbe4863d"],

Cell["\<\
The length is well short of one: the averaged state is mixed.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->194843868,ExpressionUUID->"4c678cac-5cc4-b18e-741c-25f6557603d4"],

Cell["\<\
But a conditioned trajectory, keeping the record, stays pure on the surface \
of the ball, fluctuating around that mixed average. Run one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->763032948,ExpressionUUID->"0528a095-4bdb-63f8-2cd7-39df6e6e31c2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"watched", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", "/", "2"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]dr", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "8.", ",", " ", "5"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[263]:= ",
 CellID->1903978139,ExpressionUUID->"1a78d2a2-b26e-4f45-4a07-cb0fc71b15af"],

Cell["\<\
Confirm it stays pure, reading the largest linear entropy along the whole run:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1178571435,ExpressionUUID->"316f19e5-f7db-2937-6714-90ce826e781d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
         RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "/",
      "2"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"watched", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[264]:= ",
 CellID->324779341,ExpressionUUID->"3daec99f-8291-5f2c-6b55-e0d937242276"],

Cell["The linear entropy stays at zero to rounding.", "Text",
 CellID->1319522016,ExpressionUUID->"5dea9ab6-68b8-c529-0be9-13f00932ac73"],

Cell["\<\
Now visualize the pure trajectory on the Bloch-sphere surface, with the mixed \
averaged state marked inside:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->536221529,ExpressionUUID->"030af18e-b5e5-d347-3109-e8ebc391a1ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"watched", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", "\"\<a pure trajectory circles the mixed average (black dot)\>\"", ",",
    " ", "None", ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.035", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Point", "[", "settled", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[265]:= ",
 CellID->327893574,ExpressionUUID->"405f2726-590a-86f0-7064-be8058bcecda"],

Cell["\<\
The surface path is the atom as an observer with the record sees it; the \
interior point is the atom traced over the record. Neither is more true; they \
answer different questions. This picture, a pure trajectory circling a mixed \
average, is the theme of all twenty systems.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->40368820,ExpressionUUID->"385fe069-90bd-43ce-6864-fa3321481114"],

Cell["The Mollow Triplet: Resonance-Fluorescence Spectrum", "Subsection",
 CellID->634400894,ExpressionUUID->"709f1246-ab2e-00b9-20a4-9423cedb5283"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The spectrum (power spectrum) of the light a driven atom emits, from the \
record alone. The light divides into two parts: an ",
 StyleBox["elastic", "TI"],
 " (coherent) line at the drive frequency, a delta function carrying the \
weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       StyleBox["ss",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50a39cef-8bd0-9934-0050-15c92e6ae81e"],
 ", and the ",
 StyleBox["inelastic", "TI"],
 " (fluorescence) spectrum of the fluctuations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["ss",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6eea4472-a755-a6aa-16ea-5e3fd2e10cf0"],
 ", which by quantum regression is a resolvent of the Liouvillian at the \
steady state,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1423111785,ExpressionUUID->"1d344668-2780-d87f-44cc-5832523aab45"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["inel",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
    StyleBox["Re",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "\[Mu]", "t"}], "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
       StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["ss",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->57325639,ExpressionUUID->"7ae7ede6-d60d-06a2-2a9c-04c3e3b86c88"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For weak driving the inelastic part is a single line; for strong driving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[GreaterGreater]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71444f73-786e-4642-277c-673d791b2ca8"],
 " it splits into the three-peaked ",
 StyleBox["Mollow triplet", "TI"],
 ", a central line and two sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74f6de95-8032-4c15-1c8d-d7df31c7177f"],
 ", the dynamical Stark effect."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1374945886,ExpressionUUID->"389004b5-9a2c-3ef3-68af-9dff1fde84d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Homodyne detection instead reads a chosen quadrature, and its spectrum can \
dip ",
 StyleBox["below", "TI"],
 " the shot-noise floor: squeezed, nonclassical light. Build both from the \
same big matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->456950207,ExpressionUUID->"2d697f6b-3d93-338c-5b17-7735b42781d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One last set of quantities from the master equation, all through the \
eigen-based spectrum tool built for the quantum point contact (",
 Cell[BoxData["regressionSpectrum"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a70809-2e49-b141-505c-a2534bfd03ab"],
 "). It needs no shifted frequency grid, because the steady mode is dropped \
explicitly. The inelastic fluorescence spectrum is its correlation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7723626c-4939-a85b-1ed0-843668cdfaa1"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1460592219,ExpressionUUID->"6663ba53-1d85-6946-0e10-3c1d94303bac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",", " ", "tones_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}], ",",
           " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"First", "@", 
         RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
          "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dm", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"lower", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}], " ", "id2"}]}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"regressionSpectrum", "[", 
        RowBox[{"big", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dm", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "dm", "]"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[266]:= ",
 CellID->1677337148,ExpressionUUID->"2a52a343-e04e-4391-5a61-3b2c91fb11fb"],

Cell["\<\
Sweep frequencies (centered on zero, no offset needed) for a weak and a \
strong drive:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->559816626,ExpressionUUID->"48a3001a-e719-cbe1-7850-9a4792ad99cb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tones", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], ",", " ", "9", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"weak", ",", " ", "strong"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.6", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
      RowBox[{"6.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[267]:= ",
 CellID->306702529,ExpressionUUID->"31ebe54c-d1b5-c56d-67e8-fd29e041afb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Weakly driven, the inelastic spectrum is a single line at the drive \
frequency. Strongly driven, it splits into the ",
 StyleBox["Mollow triplet",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": a central line and two sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dddb0f1-9068-854b-4be2-29bb2102ef91"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->660231635,ExpressionUUID->"4eea920a-da78-9b5c-76e9-1457dff2e9a6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now visualize the weak- and strong-drive inelastic spectra together. Their \
absolute scales differ by orders of magnitude (the weak line would vanish on \
the strong axis), so plot each normalized to its own peak to compare the ",
 StyleBox["shapes", "TI"],
 ", a single line against the triplet:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2070365498,ExpressionUUID->"7f55f164-a56a-0bbf-256a-e941cc1f5985"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"weak", "/", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "weak", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"strong", "/", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "strong", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<weak drive\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<strong drive\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "560"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency (relative to drive)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<inelastic spectrum (each / its peak)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<strong driving splits the inelastic spectrum into the Mollow \
triplet\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[268]:= ",
 CellID->1311299970,ExpressionUUID->"66a2faf2-58b3-40d9-0e51-f3bc59461223"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sidebands sit near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1685e188-3be3-a90f-3eba-f8d2bd97f855"],
 ": under strong driving the atom's levels are dressed into a four-level \
ladder, whose transitions produce the three lines. Confirm the sidebands land \
at the drive strength:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1022896615,ExpressionUUID->"1a321877-2c7f-2cce-4bc1-9231450a7614"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"tones", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FindPeaks", "[", "strong", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "6"}], "]"}], " ", "<", 
     " ", "0.6"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[269]:= ",
 CellID->1963671665,ExpressionUUID->"4421f40f-2283-9b1b-6dde-ee695737e661"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The peaks sit at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612520b5-066b-562d-10da-b9ffb31e3d77"],
 ". Confirm too that the inelastic spectrum is nowhere negative, as a genuine \
power spectrum must be:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->949858012,ExpressionUUID->"4b20a0de-bf05-fd95-7adf-39983ab1c7ff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", "strong", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[270]:= ",
 CellID->1295537244,ExpressionUUID->"4a88aa2f-b14b-d52b-7ab7-4388c0ffbc71"],

Cell["Nonnegative to rounding.", "Text",
 CellID->1775107011,ExpressionUUID->"57b69005-8bc5-b0fd-7d4d-0a6f2e7102c7"],

Cell["\<\
The elastic line lives separately, a delta at zero frequency whose weight is \
the coherent dipole; it dominates at weak drive and all but vanishes at \
strong drive as the light turns fully inelastic:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1505341139,ExpressionUUID->"72f2455d-c49b-2bf1-2282-5d06ed2e79db"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "\[CapitalOmega]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "1.", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
        RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "0.6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "6.", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[271]:= ",
 CellID->1868278770,ExpressionUUID->"77416ebe-6e08-cf7c-1d7e-87f80ba29246"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coherent weight falls by more than an order of magnitude from weak to \
strong drive. To watch the triplet being born, sweep the drive continuously \
and stack the inelastic spectra into a heatmap. The central peak dwarfs the \
sidebands at every drive, so scale each row to its own peak to keep the \
sidebands visible, and overlay the dressed-transition lines ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18599260-685f-792c-4866-144a09ea4876"],
 " as guides:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->424354000,ExpressionUUID->"32a0fa91-0c97-025a-625f-f3dba52250a0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mollowDrives", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mollowHeat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"#", "/", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "11"}], ",", " ", "11", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "mollowDrives"}], ")"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"mollowHeat", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "11"}], ",", " ", "11"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"First", "@", "mollowDrives"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Last", "@", "mollowDrives"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataReversed", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1.1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"White", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.7", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", "0.3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "0.3"}], ",", " ", "0.3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "8"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<drive \[CapitalOmega]\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the Mollow triplet is born as the drive grows (rows scaled to \
peak; \[Mu]=\[PlusMinus]\[CapitalOmega] dashed)\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[272]:= ",
 CellID->532205865,ExpressionUUID->"1d4f6d29-8280-add7-4b74-8573373af73d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bright ridge splits into three, the outer two fanning apart along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d1d4b7f-00e8-6ae3-2b23-6339b09d38c9"],
 ": the dressed-state sidebands. The triplet is what an ordinary spectrometer \
sees."
}], "Text",
 CellID->512620775,ExpressionUUID->"3b093cc2-afd1-7ed1-6936-b5afca64443b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A homodyne detector sees something an intensity spectrometer cannot: it \
measures one quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "\[Theta]"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023dde7a-8e23-336a-33c2-d0242bd781b0"],
 ", and its spectrum, normalized so the shot-noise floor is one, can fall \
below that floor. Build it from the measurement current fluctuations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->807932579,ExpressionUUID->"40fb5a43-fbb5-27db-7099-5c2cfe418d21"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",", " ", "\[Theta]_", ",", 
     " ", "tones_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "big", ",", " ", "rss", ",", " ", "cth", ",", " ", "mq", ",", " ", 
       "mean"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "c", "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "c", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"cth", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mq", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cth", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cth", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mean", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"mq", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"regressionSpectrum", "[", 
        RowBox[{"big", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cth", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rss", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cth", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"mean", " ", "rss"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mq", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"mean", " ", "id2"}]}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[273]:= ",
 CellID->243295841,ExpressionUUID->"2425f502-e1b1-2adc-4dda-ed6f90447826"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At weak drive, one quadrature is squeezed and the perpendicular one is not. \
Compare the two at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", "0.25", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "212476b8-b137-7f4a-50dc-6fe5c0c24590"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->416937359,ExpressionUUID->"3db10d53-0e34-1357-6b4e-a51dabc161bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "tones"}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<squeezed quadrature (\[Theta] = \[Pi]/2)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<anti-squeezed (\[Theta] = 0)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.7", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "560"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<homodyne spectrum / shot noise\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<resonance fluorescence dips below the shot-noise floor\>\""}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[274]:= ",
 CellID->1706026672,ExpressionUUID->"3e4bd926-69e3-4ee0-6648-d0800f9614ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57d10123-a1d4-e454-7dee-988cd066cebe"],
 " quadrature dips below the dashed shot-noise line while its partner rises \
above it: the atom's fluorescence is squeezed, its noise pushed below the \
vacuum in one quadrature at the cost of excess in the other. Confirm the dip \
is real:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1235325005,ExpressionUUID->"27645c90-4345-b83d-4d1c-55da76f10b07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
  RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[275]:= ",
 CellID->883233490,ExpressionUUID->"245848e5-b774-8ea9-4c78-61cec206d4f3"],

Cell["\<\
Below one: sub-shot-noise, a signature of nonclassical light that only \
phase-sensitive (homodyne) detection can reveal, and that the \
necessarily-nonnegative intensity spectrum of the triplet can never show. The \
whole spectroscopy, elastic line, inelastic triplet, and squeezing dip, comes \
from the two-time correlations of the same master equation built on the first \
page.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->795056725,ExpressionUUID->"0581f938-6b6a-81e3-33be-f1620e1cd3c9"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Section",
 CellID->1402288582,ExpressionUUID->"7e58b706-7f01-9af1-2667-2f607ab5e8db"],

Cell["\<\
From plain matrices and a few rules, we built a small laboratory for open \
quantum systems: the master equation for the unconditioned average, the \
positivity-preserving step for a kept record, and plotters for the Bloch \
sphere, phase space, the covariance ellipse, and spectra. On that base, \
twenty systems: pure dephasing, a driven damped atom, a cavity cat decohering \
at a rate set by the square of its separation, the Haroche experiment, \
dispersive qubit readout, quantum Brownian motion, the \
jump/homodyne/heterodyne unravellings, the quantum Zeno effect, a charge \
qubit read by a quantum point contact, measurement-induced collapse, a \
quantum Kalman filter, measurement feedback, thermalization, rapid \
purification, feedback cooling, the linear-vs-nonlinear trajectory, and the \
Mollow triplet. One theme runs through all of them: keeping the record turns \
the master equation's average into a pure, jagged, individual trajectory, and \
averaging the trajectories back recovers the master equation. Change a number \
in any cell and watch it move.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->155652986,ExpressionUUID->"0b1945ac-ce61-156f-3927-5c09eb147fb5"]
},
